            <div xml:id="d377">

                <pb facs="0473" n="375" sameAs="frus:frus1920v01/pg375"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">824.00/62: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in Bolivia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Maginnis</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-07-20T17:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">July 20, 1920—5
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>47. Your July 17, 3 p.m., and July 18, 3 p.m.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d377-f1"/></p>
                <p>The Department desires to impress upon you the necessity of exercising utmost
                    discretion in communicating with revolutionary Government. Your dealing with
                    Junta should be limited to entirely unofficial and informal intercourse, and you
                    should confine your representations to questions affecting the interests of the
                    United States and the security of American life and property, bearing in mind
                    the fact that the Government of the United States has not as yet recognized the
                    revolutionary Government as being even a <hi rendition="#italic">de facto</hi>
                    government.</p>
                <p>Report immediately any recognition of revolutionary Government by any other
                    government.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Colby</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
